<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="3asld-0-0"><span data-offset-key="3asld-0-0">Noted for throaty, yearning vocals that accompany his swimmy indie soul-pop, Yellow Days is the performance alias of British musician George van den Broek. After some early releases during his teenage years, he began to gain traction with 2017’s full-length Is Everything Okay in Your World? Switching locales to Los Angeles, his follow-up, A Day in a Yellow Beat, appeared in 2020. Two years later, the pandemic-inspired EP trilogy Slow Dance &amp; Romance, Apple Pie, and Inner Peace was steeped in psychedelic soul.</span></div>
