<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="6mjg-0-0"><span data-offset-key="6mjg-0-0">Her breakout “En Repeat” introduced a genre-bending sound built on reggaeton rhythms, haunting tonal shifts, and percussion that mirrors the rise and collapse of hope. She followed with “The Holy Trinity,” a daring exploration of desire, identity, and queer awakening—part club confession, part coming-out anthem—backed by lush disco strings, pulsing electronic drums, and fearless vocals. Grace continued to expand her sonic range with “Everything Reminds Me of You,” a 185 BPM indie-rock rush capturing love’s haunting grip across New York City, and “Super Elastic,” a cinematic dance-pop powerhouse of thunderous synths and operatic vocal lines.</span></div>
<div data-offset-key="6mjg-0-0">-</div>
</div>
<div class="" data-block="true" data-editor="bj3ds" data-offset-key="d14qg-0-0">
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="d14qg-0-0"><span data-offset-key="d14qg-0-0">With “Curtains,” she delivered her most theatrical work yet: a haunting waltz arranged for a live string quartet, where every lyric lands like a final bow in a love story’s last act.</span></div>
<div data-offset-key="d14qg-0-0">-</div>
</div>
<div class="" data-block="true" data-editor="bj3ds" data-offset-key="vucr-0-0">
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="vucr-0-0"><span data-offset-key="vucr-0-0">Her orchestral reimagining of The Cranberries’ “Zombie” further demonstrates her artistry, transforming the iconic protest anthem into a brooding, emotionally synth explosive ballad. Most recently, “Lucky You’re A Star” showcases her maximalist, euphoric Euro-pop side.</span></div>
<div data-offset-key="vucr-0-0">-</div>
</div>
<div class="" data-block="true" data-editor="bj3ds" data-offset-key="12u4l-0-0">
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="12u4l-0-0"><span data-offset-key="12u4l-0-0">Valencia Grace has captivated audiences on some of the world’s biggest stages, including Austin City Limits, Lollapalooza Chicago, Outside Lands, Hyde Park BST, and more. She is now bringing her bold vision to the stage with SUPER ELASTIC: A POP OPERA in March 2026, hitting Boston, Brooklyn, Philadelphia, and Washington, D.C. With each release and now her first headlining shows, she continues to cement her place as one of pop’s most fearless, visionary new voices.</span></div>
<div data-offset-key="12u4l-0-0">-</div>
<div data-offset-key="12u4l-0-0">[embedyt] https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z8EztQ7Vjxk[/embedyt]</div>
<div data-offset-key="12u4l-0-0">-</div>
<div data-offset-key="12u4l-0-0"><span data-huuid="16968643104058488171">James the Seventh is a <mark class="QVRyCf">self-taught singer, songwriter, producer, and musician from Philadelphia</mark> who creates a dark and atmospheric style of alternative pop. </span><span data-huuid="16968643104058488814">Her songs feature raw lyrics over emotive melodies. </span><span data-huuid="16968643104058489457">James the Seventh once aspired to become a professional ballet dancer, starting online school at age 13. However, an injury led her to find a new calling in music after her father bought her a guitar</span>.</div>
</div>"
