<em><strong>* MOVED TO 4/16, ALL TICKETS HONORED *</strong></em>

After a whirlwind year of globetrotting, with electrifying performances across Europe and Mexico, SIX SEX has cemented herself as a force in the global electronic music scene. Named by Rolling Stone and NME as one of the essential artists to watch in 2025, this Argentine club queen continues to push boundaries and captivate audiences around the world.

Known for his bold live shows, SIX SEX blends energetic club beats with a theatrical flair that leaves audiences mesmerized. Every stage she performs transforms into a visceral rave—a cathartic blend of liberation, performance, and raw energy. In recent years, she has collaborated with producers from the vibrant Latin Club scene as well as Berlin's electronic avant-garde, further expanding her sonic universe.

Her highly anticipated new EP, X-sex, is a showcase of electronic euphoria, pop excellence, and overflowing attitude, featuring some of the most provocative tracks of his career. As usual, SIX SEX has assembled a dream team of international electronic producers—Luca Eck, Dauner, David Jackson, Pablo Bozzi, Bbynito, MCR-T, DJ g2g, and DBBD—to create an EP that further deepens the rave intensity he explored on his acclaimed previous EP, SATISFIRE. After being recognized by Rolling Stone and NME as one of the essential artists to follow in 2025, X-sex arrives to reaffirm this status.

The EP begins with the iconic squat tutorial "How to Make Your Ass Bigger," setting the tone for what follows: an invitation to dance and fantasy. "Performance Actitud (Pose)" captures the moment when the music takes over the body and dancing is all that matters. Meanwhile, "Bitches Like Me" is a sassy, attitude-filled anthem, perfect for enjoying with friends. The second half of the EP takes on a more erotic tone, beginning with a guest appearance by Argentinian rapper Dillom on "Tócame," where the two engage in an uncensored dirty talk duel. The screams of pleasure and catharsis in "Ahhhhhh" and the polyamory anthem "U&amp;ME" form the climax of X-sex, proving once again that SIX SEX is unafraid to explore the limits of provocation and desire.

In November 2024, SIX SEX made a triumphant debut at Berlin's iconic Berghain—a true sanctuary of rave culture—reinforcing her connection to the roots of electronic music. Looking ahead to 2025, she already has a performance scheduled at the prestigious Sónar Festival in Barcelona, Boiler Room in Ibiza and will embark on her highly anticipated debut USA tour. See you on the dance floor.

