  string(5245) "-
<div class="" data-block="true" data-editor="6qgj8" data-offset-key="75hnk-0-0">
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="75hnk-0-0"><span data-offset-key="75hnk-0-0">Getdown Services are Josh Law and Ben Sadler, childhood friends from Minehead, Somerset, now based in Bristol. Together they make sharp, groove-driven music that mixes post-punk, funk and social commentary with dry humour and astute observations of everyday life.</span></div>
<div data-offset-key="75hnk-0-0">-</div>
</div>
<div class="" data-block="true" data-editor="6qgj8" data-offset-key="fg1og-0-0">
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="fg1og-0-0"><span data-offset-key="fg1og-0-0">Their debut album Crisps (Breakfast Records, 2023) introduced a sound rooted in rhythm, wit and working-class surrealism. Songs about modern Britain were set to arrangements that reflected both their humour and frustration. The album drew praise for its originality and set the tone for everything that has since followed.</span></div>
<div data-offset-key="fg1og-0-0">-</div>
</div>
<div class="" data-block="true" data-editor="6qgj8" data-offset-key="cofjs-0-0">
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="cofjs-0-0"><span data-offset-key="cofjs-0-0">Since then, Getdown Services have built a reputation as one of the most entertaining and distinctive live bands in the UK. Their second EP Your Medal’s In The Post (2024) received support from Rolling Stone UK, DIY, The Line of Best Fit, Clash and BBC 6Music, and fan favourite Dog Dribble was playlisted by BBCMusic. The release was followed by a sold-out UK headline tour and a first European run in early 2025.</span></div>
<div data-offset-key="cofjs-0-0">-</div>
</div>
<div class="" data-block="true" data-editor="6qgj8" data-offset-key="10fbk-0-0">
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="10fbk-0-0"><span data-offset-key="10fbk-0-0">The following year brought Primordial Slot Machine, a six-track EP led by Eat Quiche, Sleep, Repeat. It saw the pair exploring themes of self-doubt and acceptance through their trademark mix of humour and pathos. Festival appearances at Glastonbury, Green Man, End of the Road, Wide Awake, The Great Escape and Live at Leeds drew huge crowds, alongside a live performance on the BBC. Off the back of these, the band’s two headline nights at London’s Electric Ballroom sold out almost immediately.</span></div>
</div>
<div class="" data-block="true" data-editor="6qgj8" data-offset-key="4s3h7-0-0">
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="4s3h7-0-0"><span data-offset-key="4s3h7-0-0">In November 2025, Getdown Services will release Crumbs 2, a companion to the previous year’s Crumbs, collecting demos and B-sides that offered a glimpse into their writing process.</span></div>
<div data-offset-key="4s3h7-0-0">-</div>
</div>
<div class="" data-block="true" data-editor="6qgj8" data-offset-key="6je52-0-0">
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="6je52-0-0"><span data-offset-key="6je52-0-0">The band’s 2025 UK and European headline tour is completely sold out and includes two nights at Bristol’s Trinity Centre, two at London’s Electric Ballroom, and a spring 2026 run supporting Viagra Boys, including shows at Alexandra Palace and Paradiso, Amsterdam.</span></div>
<div data-offset-key="6je52-0-0">-</div>
</div>
<div class="" data-block="true" data-editor="6qgj8" data-offset-key="ffrbv-0-0">
<div class="public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr" data-offset-key="ffrbv-0-0"><span data-offset-key="ffrbv-0-0">With consistent support from Rolling Stone UK, The Observer, DIY, So Young, The Line of Best Fit and BBC 6Music to name just a few, Getdown Services have become a fixture in the UK’s independent scene. Their approach - completely DIY and testament to both hard work and innate talent - continues to make them one of the most original and exciting voices in British music.</span></div>
<div data-offset-key="ffrbv-0-0">-</div>
<div data-offset-key="ffrbv-0-0">[embedyt] https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HjXAfhP8RkY[/embedyt]</div>
<div data-offset-key="ffrbv-0-0">-</div>
<div data-offset-key="ffrbv-0-0">

My name is Darren Keen. I am from Chicago and I do the one person band called PROBLEMS.

PROBLEMS Has toured Europe, New Zealand, and America extensively. I have opened for Peaches, Dan Deacon, Pile, death's dynamic shroud, Mezerg, Lightning Bolt, Wolf Eyes, Plack Blague, and many others. I have played at Meow Wolf in Denver, and several fests including Camp A Low Hum (NZ), Laektro (DK), No Coast Fest (TX), UIUI Fest (Amsterdam) and the Petfest and Lincoln Calling fests in Nebraska.

My new 12” LP “Enter The Annals” was released this year on The Record Machine. I have previously worked with Orange Milk Records and Geertruida (NL).

I make composer driven electronic music with live vocals that is sometimes very fun and is sometimes very beautiful and is always interesting

</div>
